This folder contains programs that are useful in
processing SiB4 output.

-----FORTRAN ROUTINES---------------
All the routines in this folder use netcdf,
and are included in the Makefile.  
To change the location of netcdf libraries,
modify the Makefile.

All of these routines can be used using the
program 'sib4post'.  To make this program,
simply type:
>make sib4post

To run any program, for any program edit
the associated ".txt" file, and then type:
>sib4post routine
where routine is the routine name
(before the "_").

For example, to balance fluxes, edit the 
balance.txt file and then run:
>sib4post balance

If not using 'sib4post', all routines can also
be run individually.  All routines are compiled
by just typing 'make'.  Each routine can be 
compiled individually by typing:
>make routine
(routine name before the "_").
Note: To use the individual routines, most of them
do not use the ".txt" input file, but rather 
need the information specified in the file
directly (such as in balance_sib.f90).  
Then to get that information, the routine
will need to be recompiled.  This is useful
to "hardwire" in specific files/information.

COMPRESSION:
Most of the routines have the commands included to 
compress the output.  For some of the routines,
these commands are currently commented out.  
To use, you will need to switch the ncdf_create to 
use hdf5 (not 64bit), and you will need to uncomment
the call to ncdf_def_var_deflate.  For newer routines,
there is a switch in sibinfo_module.f90 that switches
between compressed and non-compressed files.  To create
compressed files, set use_deflate=.TRUE.

MULTIPLE YEARS:
To post-process multiple years, processing each
year individually on a separate processor,
use the perl script sib4post.pl.  
To use, make the changes in the program's
input file (xxx.txt), then specify the
program and the years to process.
For example, to merge 1997 through 2017:
>sib4post.pl merge 1997 2017

======================================================
Brief descriptions of all the files are listed below.
More information is in the README_procsteps file.
------------------------------------------------------

addresp
------------
Adds the balanced respiration, saved in a single
ratio file, into new output files.

balance
--------
Balances the non-crop PFTs by scaling the respiration.
Assumes monthly SiB4 output files (hsib/psib/qsib).
Creates either a single file with the ratios,
   or adds the balanced respiration to the files.


checkbal
--------
Checks the balance of the fluxes.
Allows for either the balanced respiration
to be included in the output files or 
to be read from the ratio file.
Expects a crop harvest distribution file,
otherwise this information is not used.


combine
-------
Combines plant functional types
to create gridcell means.


conjoin
-------
Conjoins multiple output files into
a single netcdf file.

For example, combines monthly files into
a single annual file.

Conjoins both land unit and gridcell files.

Currently checks for eight required variables
in the output file without specifying them in 
the user options:
   - Longitude, latitude, pft_names, pft_refs,
     lu_area, lu_pref, site_names, and time
   - If these are not found, they are ignored


cropdist
--------
Redistributes the crop carbon removed during harvest.
Uses a crop distribution map for spatial 
   distribution of the crop flux.
Uses a region definition map to keep specified percentage
   of crop carbon domestic, rather than international.
   - Set to 90% in the sibinfo_module
      (variable name regionfrac)
   - Currently assumes the region map is transcom regions,
     with 11 land and 11 ocean regions.
Assumes the input files are monthly files.
Currently processes only vector formats.


disjoin
-------
Disjoins monthly files, breaking them apart
into daily files.
Should work for both vector and grid output.


gpptot
-------
Program to calculate the total GPP over 
the time specified.
Prints to screen the calculated global annual GPP,
   and optional output of the GPP distributed
   by biome and by PFT.

grid
----
Program to put SiB4 vector output files
onto a grid.
Creates a new file containing the gridded output.
If the file is a SiB4 diagnostic, the new filename
  is changed from "sib" to "grid"

meanclim
--------
Program to create an annual mean SiB4 file.
Assumes the input files are monthly diagnostic
   output files.
Assumes at least two years are being combined.
Creates a new file containing the mean values for
   a single year.
   - New filename has the last two digits of the
     starting and stopping months.

merge
-----
Merges the output files from simulations that were split 
into sections for running on multiple processors.
Creates new files, without the "pxxx" indicators.
It contains the option to write out only select variables.
If you wish to merge all variables, then set the
integer below the line stating "number of variables" to -1.
If you wish to merge only a subset of variables, then set
the integer to the number you wish, followed by a list of
the variable names to be merged.  Even if you wish to
only save a single variable, this routine rently requires 
eight variables for information (which can be changed in
sibinfo_module.f90).


pullvar
--------
Pulls out specific variables from a netcdf file,
   creating a new file containing only the
   specified variables.
Processes any netcdf file (vector or gridded formats)

Currently requires eight variables to be included 
in the output file without specifying them in 
the user options:
   - Longitude, latitude, pft_names, pft_refs,
     lu_area, lu_pref, site_names, and time
   - If these are not found, they are ignored


regrid
------
Regrids already gridded output.
Assumes all lats/lons are grid centers.
Creates new files
   --By default, the new filename will
     include the resolution
   --Specific prefix text can be specified
     in the input/output paths


renamevar
---------
Renames specific variables, and also has the
    capability to change the associated attributes
    --Long_name, title, and units


replaceresp
------------
Program to replace the original respiration (resp_tot)
with balanced respiration (resp_bal).  Create new files.


unstack
--------
Unstacks the PFTs, creating single levels
for each PFT (rather than the limited 10 
land units).  While unstacking, it has the 
option to add the balanced repsiration
as well as the redistributed crop harvest
respiration.  Creates CF-compiliant output.


sibinfo_module.f90
------------------
Module file containing SiB4-specific information.
Includes:
   - Diagnostic output information (prefix/suffix)
   - Dimension names
   - Specific variables names
   - Flux variable names
   - PFT information (number/names/references)
   - Biome information (names/references)
   - Common formats

sibinfo_tools.f90
-------------------
File that contains generic subroutines to process
   netcdf files.

======================================================
Overview of the order of routines in sib4post
------------------------------------------------------

sib4post.f90 --> sib4post_process.f90 --> sib4post_parse.f90
  --> sib4post_control.f90  --> individual routines


sib4post.f90
-------------
-- parses the routine called after sib4post

sib4post_process.f90
----------------------
-- reads the input files
-- calls sib4post_parse with appropriate options
   for sib4 output
-- calls sib4post_control for specific files
   that do not need filename parsing

sib4post_parse.f90
-------------------
-- parses the file name options and creates all
   input and output filenames

sib4post_control.f90
--------------------
-- calls the appropriate routine with all filenames
    and options


